:"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C026\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States the fund 'can deliver low-basis securities in kind rather than selling them for cash' and that under IRC §852(b)(6) 'a RIC recognizes no gain on that in-kind distribution.'\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says the fund 'can purge its most appreciated lots without realizing gains,' which reduces embedded gains, and contrasts this with mutual funds whose cash-redemption sales 'can generate capital gain distributions passed to all remaining shareholders.'\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says 'Your own sale of ETF shares is still taxable,' that the result is 'deferral, not permanent,' and that cash redemptions and rebalancing or index-change sales 'can still realize gains,' so distributions are not ruled out.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"The answer meets all three required minimums: fund-level nonrecognition on in-kind transfers, removal of low-basis lots reducing distributions versus cash-redeeming funds, and clear limits (no absolute exemption, investor sale taxable, deferral only, depends on in-kind transactions). It contains no central error and no material local falsehood.\"}","ttft_ms":4024,"type":"result","duration_ms":7321,"uuid":"9889f5bd-c6be-42cb-a0e8-854524eae767","ttft_stream_ms":1089,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":1089,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
